---
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import DocumentLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.aiReliability;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<DocumentLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <ContentCard>
<p class="section-kicker">Human, agent, and mixed-team investigations</p>
    <h2>A common record across investigator types</h2>
    <p>TENSOR uses the same question, evidence, assessment, and decision model for people and agents. An agent can participate in an investigation, be the subject of one, or occupy different roles in different contexts.</p>
    <p>Attribution identifies the actor responsible for an entry. Question context identifies the subject, time, and parameters being assessed. These roles remain explicit during a handoff.</p>
    <h2>Recorded claims</h2>
    <table><thead><tr><th>Entry</th><th>Agent-transfer example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Observation</td><td>A tool-call log records an outbound request.</td></tr><tr><td>Assessment</td><td>The available evidence initially leaves the transmitted content unknown.</td></tr><tr><td>Decision</td><td>An investigator records a collection decision and its policy context.</td></tr><tr><td>Action record</td><td>A collection operation is reported as planned, attempted, or completed.</td></tr></tbody></table>
    <p>An assessment records its rationale, method, and evidence inputs. Confidence values include a scale and interpretation. The contract does not require disclosure of private model reasoning.</p>
    <h2>Disagreement and revision</h2>
    <p>Competing assessments retain their own evidence and attribution. A decision explicitly selects the assessment used for a transition. New evidence produces a revision with retained earlier inputs and a review of affected decisions.</p>
    <p>Missing evidence can remain unknown. Recorded history supports examination of a decision even when a model run cannot be reproduced exactly.</p>
    <h2>Policy and authority</h2>
    <p>Policy references and authority assertions are distinct entries. The surrounding vendor or organization system enforces evidence access, delegation, and execution permissions. Import and validation are data operations; they do not retrieve evidence or execute recorded actions.</p>
    <h2>Reference cases</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/investigation-lab/">Investigation Lab</a> includes an agent-transfer case led by a human and an identity case prepared with agent assistance. Both use fictional evidence and the same Core binding.</p>
    <p><a href="/core/">Core contract</a> · <a href="/extensions/">Vendor and organization layers</a> · <a href="/conformance/">Validation</a></p>
  </ContentCard>
</DocumentLayout>
